  "sanity": {
    "note": "A price too good to be true usually is: a parsing error, a mis-mapped cabin, or a fare for a different journey. Phase 5 showed how convincing a fabricated candidate looks, so implausible values are FLAGGED AND STORED with a diagnostic reason rather than discarded - a silent drop hides a provider that has started returning nonsense. CALIBRATION: these floors must catch the IMPOSSIBLE, not the merely remarkable. The whole point of the radar is finding fares nobody expects, so a floor set at 'a really good business fare' would reject exactly what it exists to find. A 600 EUR business fare to Bangkok is a legendary mistake fare; a 12 EUR one is a bug. The floors sit between those.",
